"timestamp": "2026-04-06T13:42:49Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "11. The visual identity of this production was defined by a massive, 27-foot-diameter revolving turntable that allowed for cinematic cross-fades between the gritty streets of the rebellion and the internal monologues of the characters. While it became a global titan, the English-language version almost never happened; the original 1980 French concept album had a short run in a sports arena, and British producer Cameron Mackintosh only agreed to develop it after hearing a tape of the \"Red and Black\" anthem.", "role": "hint", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]